  "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta =\\frac{1}{2},$ where $\\theta =m\u2220A.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{\u2015}{BC}$ opposite to $\u2220A.$ Hence, we can use the sine ratio to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{8}{AB} \\\\ AB & =8(2) \\\\ AB & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the missing side $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}-B{C}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{16}^{2}-{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{256-64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{192} \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\u25b3ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\cdot (8\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =32\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
